Long original clock recordings repeat the same DWORD during busy waits. Accept
an optional DD2TKR1 run container with DD2_TICK_REPLAY_FORMAT=DD2TKR1. Each run
stores one little-endian value/count pair; every original call still returns
exactly one value, increments the logical call counter and pumps audio services
at the same positions. The explicit format leaves every legacy raw DWORD
sequence unchanged, even values resembling a header. Reject partial,
zero/overflowing runs and leftovers including an unfinished final run. This
changes comparison input storage, not live timing or original/port parity.

